#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/intel_modeset_setup.c (new overlay; the full file, derived from drm-kmod's display/intel_modeset_setup.c)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0022-core-k1-staged-edp-takeover.patch
#
# Why: scaled resolutions and 240 Hz (HBR3 + DSC) need i915 to own the eDP pipe; today the firmware raster is
# kept and only PLANE_SURF is flipped.  Like NVKMS keeping the boot raster before NVRMFB commits a mode, the
# takeover is staged; K1 adopts read-only.  NVRAM xegfx-disp-kms=1 (claim boots only) runs the real display
# (disable_display=0, no_display=0, i915_xegfx_kms=1); non-internal VBT children are dropped so only eDP is set
# up; setup_hw_state reads out and takes the active pipe's power references but skips every sanitize; no
# initial plane config, wm sanitize, initial commit, hotplug, fbdev or OpRegion registration.  The connector,
# eDP caps, fixed modes and crtc readout go to debug.xegfx_disp.  Without the NVRAM key behaviour is unchanged.
# Status: built and installed, not yet run on hardware.
#
